# A uniform value below a geometric bound: n is geometric, Pr[n = k] = 2^-(k+1), and x is uniform on
# {0, …, n}, so Pr[n = k, x = j] = 2^-(k+1) / (k + 1) for j ≤ k.
#
# The bound n takes infinitely many values, so unif(0, n) cannot be computed by a case split over them.
# Prodigy computes it on the generating function G of n (#385): appending 1 + x + … + x^k to every term n^k is
# the substitution (G(n) - x·G(n·x))/(1 - x), and the weight 1/(k + 1) is the operator 1/(θ + 1) with
# θ = n·∂/∂n, i.e. (1/n)·∫_0^n. The integral is proposed and certified by its derivative and its value at 0;
# here the result is log((2 - n·x)/(2 - n)) / (n (1 - x)).

n: nat = geometric(1/2);  # the bound
x: nat = unif(0, n);  # uniform on {0, …, n}
query Pr[x == 0];  # expected: log(2) ≈ 0.6931
query Pr[x == 1];  # expected: log(2) - 1/2 ≈ 0.1931
query Ex[x];  # expected: Ex[n]/2 = 1/2
query Pr[n == 2 and x == 1];  # expected: 1/8 · 1/3 = 1/24
